  "solution": {
    "text": "The copper(I) sulphide produced is converted to copper with a final blast of air. The end product of this is called blister copper - a porous brittle form of copper, about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>98</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> pure. The reactions given are carried out in the production of blister copper using self reduction.",
